error[consumed_borrowed_handle]: `g5_close` ends the life of what it is given, and `h` was borrowed — this function promised not to change it
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-2242-a-lent-parameter-ended-is-told-to-drop-its-lent.hero:15:21
     |
  15 |     return g5_close(h)  #~ consumed_borrowed_handle
     |                     ^
  note: a parameter written without `@` is borrowed: the caller keeps the value and reads it again after the call, so a call that frees it leaves them holding an address C has taken back. Write the parameter `@h` in the signature of `ended`, without its `lent`, and `@` before its argument at every call of `ended`, which says on both lines that the value does not survive; this call stays as it is, since `g5_close` takes this argument without `@`
  note: this refuses the call, not the copy: a copy made BEFORE the call still holds the freed address, and nothing here sees that. design.md Part 8 wart 20 states that cost and names what would close it
